<title>UK: Gehe's AAH sells Belfast depot.</title>
<headline>Gehe's AAH sells Belfast depot.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>AAH, the British arm of German pharmaceutical wholesaler Gehe AG, said on Friday that it has sold its Belfast Daniels depot to Irish pharmaceutical distibution firm United Drug Plc.</p>
<p>It said in a statement that the sale, for an undisclosed amount, is the first step in a series of disposals demanded by the Monopolies and Mergers Commission (MMC) as part of its conditional acceptance of AAH's merger with Lloyds Chemists Plc.</p>
<p>Under the terms of the MMC's agreement another six depots are to be sold. &quot;The sale of the six remaining depots is progressing in line with the MMC's timetable and there are a number of potential buyers at the table,&quot; said the company.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
</text>
